#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# residue

#% text
# `residue(f, [x, a])` gives the residue of `f` at `x = a`: the coefficient of `1/(x - a)` in its Laurent expansion (poles up to order 7).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
residue(1/(x*(x - 1)), [x, 0])
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
residue(exp(x)/x^3, [x, 0])
#% output
#= 1/2

#% cell
residue(1/(x^2 + 1), [x, sqrt(-1)])
#% output
#= -im/2

